<!--Post: 6738--><!--Time: 1107991406-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6738"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 3:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Agreed.   It would leave a traceable connection.  He could attempt to do it at a library, or an office building, or internet cafe, but even then there would be too many people around.   <BR> <BR>The only safe communication is drop-off communication.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
