<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6761"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 5:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->When the Rooster crows could perhaps mean...right before the end sun is up ...signifying a new day...meaning at the end of the year of the rooster?  Who knows...just a thought... <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
