<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6794"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 8:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think Tom V´s pride makes him do EVERYTHING possible to avoid that som prankmoron is filling up the &#34;from BTK&#34; thred, belive me that thred is not just another thred to Tom IMO<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6794-->
<!--Post: 6826--><!--Time: 1108023432-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6826"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 12:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You&#39;re right, Skov. I&#39;m not ripping on Tom, or anyone else on this site---except those posters. My point is just my point. I don&#39;t believe any of those cats are the real thing. And there&#39;s no way to know. But they can&#39;t all be real. Maybe the real one will visit this thread to defend himself.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6826-->
<!--Post: 6914--><!--Time: 1108073751-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6914"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 2:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sherlock, <BR> <BR>Even if there is some “secret symbol” to validate BTK, I’m beginning to worry that some of these drops may not be authentic either.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6914-->
<!--Post: 6919--><!--Time: 1108076576-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6919"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 3:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ooh, Iceteajan, can you say more about your hunch that some of the drops may be hoaxes? Does anything in particular fuel your thinking? <BR> <BR>I also started a thread under Theories: &#39;BTK is D-E-A-D&#39; <BR>The idea is that it&#39;s not BTK making the drops but rather someone who came into possession of his &#39;treasure trove&#39; <BR>There are some very interesting quotes there from posters with far greater knowledge of the case than me.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6919-->
<!--Post: 6935--><!--Time: 1108083348-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6935"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 4:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sherlock, <BR> <BR>I really wonder if BTK is being DRAWN OUT &#40;by the authorities&#41; using bogus, intermittent, drops? <BR> <BR>These bogus drops may infuriate BTK, who in turn would need to keep “stepping into the limelight” bearing his own legitimate proof &#40;souvenirs&#41;, and taking proper due credit about his misdeeds. <BR> <BR>To me the equation is simple:  more drops =  more clues.  Even the tiniest microscopic bit of residue on the postcard may be specific to an area or occupation -- and thereby corner him. <BR> <BR>Remember the Patty Hearst kidnapping?   There were birds chirping in the background of the kidnappers’ tape recording.  The tape was studied by someone in the know about birds.  They found that these birds were indigenous to only one specific area in California.   <BR> <BR>This didn’t solve the kidnapping because they were constantly on the move, but you get the idea about how something so inconspicuous can turn into something very useful.   <BR> <BR>I think BTK is incredibly foolish to continue making these drops.  With forenic science, traffic cameras, night vision binoculars, etc. -- he is bound to be cornered.   <BR> <BR>They MAY already have a good idea about who it is.  Why?  Because the swabbings that are going on might only be for “eliminations” – not for prosecution.   <BR> <BR>If they’ve narrowed down say 20 suspects, and 15 agreed to be swabbed, then they need focus on the other 5 more seriously. <BR> <BR>THEY MUST HAVE HAD SOME DISTINGUISHING DATA THAT MADE THEM SWAB SOME PEOPLE. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6935-->
<!--Post: 6962--><!--Time: 1108095733-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6962"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 8:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Brilliant! I am speaking of what you say all the way through &#34;he is bound to be cornered.&#34; I think you may very well be right. <BR> <BR>After that my thinking is different. I don&#39;t think the police have DNA that will do them any good. It could just be a bluff and they don&#39;t have any DNA period. If they do, though, then that is where my theory comes in that someone other than the real killer is behind all this and he has nothing at all to fear from a swabbing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6962-->
<!--Post: 6971--><!--Time: 1108099000-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6971"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Toto<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Toto<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 9:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ditto on the Brilliant! If it&#39;s not LE making &#39;phony&#39; drops, then they should be!  Hope they&#39;re reading the board.  That is exactly the type of thing that would bring BTK out, even if just to refute the evidence and once again prove LE&#39;s ineptness.   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6971-->
<!--Post: 6984--><!--Time: 1108107907-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6984"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 11:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What does LE stand for? Wichita PD?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6984-->
<!--Post: 7003--><!--Time: 1108121486-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7003"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Haytrader<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Haytrader<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 3:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sherlock. <BR> <BR>LE means law enforcment.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
